  "articleBody": "When you're accused of a crime, it can feel like your world has been turned upside down, and you might not know what to do next. It's a really serious situation, and your actions immediately following an accusation can have a big impact on your future. The most crucial thing is to remain calm and remember your rights. Anything you say can be used against you, so it's always best to exercise your right to remain silent until you've spoken with legal counsel. Don't try to explain your side to the police without an attorney present; their job is to investigate, and even innocent statements can be misunderstood or twisted. Also, avoid discussing your case with anyone else, including friends or family, because those conversations aren't protected. Getting an experienced criminal defense lawyer involved right away is your best move. They can explain the charges against you, advise you on how to proceed, and start building a strong defense to protect your rights from the very beginning, whether you're facing a misdemeanor or a serious felony.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-26"
